ator-dot","content":"Indicator dot"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-14","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-15","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"When to Use"},"1171":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-16","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1172":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-17","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#props","content":"Props"},"1173":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#default","content":"A minimal tag with the default emphasis and size."},"1174":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-19","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#emphasis","content":"Nine emphasis options are available. Choose the one that fits the visual tone of your context."},"1175":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-20","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#sizes","content":"Choose a size that fits the surrounding content. Smaller tags work well in compact layouts like tables; larger tags suit headings or hero sections."},"1176":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-21","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#inline","content":"Use `design=\"inline\"` to embed a tag within a sentence. The background and border are removed so the tag blends into the text flow."},"1177":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-22","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#high-contrast","content":"A bolder color treatment for when tags need to stand out more - for example, on colored backgrounds."},"1178":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-23","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#with-icon","content":"Icons reinforce the tag's meaning at a glance. Add an `Icon` as a child - it inherits the tag's color and scales with its size."},"1179":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-24","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator","content":"A minimal style that pairs a small colored dot with a neutral background. Well suited for dense layouts like tables or dashboards where multiple tags in close proximity would otherwise compete for attention."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#screen-readers","content":"Tags are `<span>` elements with no special ARIA role. Screen readers announce the tag's text as part of normal page content — no extra markup is needed."},"1181":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-26","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#decorative-icons","content":"Icons passed as children must include `aria-hidden=\"true\"` so they are skipped by screen readers. The text label is the sole carrier of meaning."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator-dot","content":"The colored dot is decorative and invisible to screen readers. The text label must convey the status on its own — never rely on the dot alone to communicate meaning."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the indicator style in dense layouts like tables and dashboards. Use the filled style when the tag is a prominent, standalone element on a card or hero section."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Default to the small size in compact layouts like tables and lists. Use medium or large only when the tag needs to stand out as a primary piece of information."},"1185":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the inline design only within running prose. In grouped or standalone contexts, the filled style provides better visual separation."},"1186":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple tags of different emphasis on the same item. Choose the most important one — too many competing labels lose their meaning."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Showing the status of an item on a card, table row, or list entry (e.g. \"Active\", \"Expired\", \"Pending\")"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-33","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Categorizing or grouping content so users can scan and filter quickly (e.g. \"New\", \"Sale\", \"Beta\")"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-34","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Surfacing metadata about an item (e.g. \"Pro\", \"Free trial\", \"Internal\")"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-35","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Communicating priority or category in project management and collaboration tools (e.g. \"High priority\", \"In review\")"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-36","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"If users need to click or dismiss it — use a **Button** instead."},"1192":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-37","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"If the label is part of a sentence with no visual distinction — just use text."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"page","content":"TextField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field","content":"TextField is a single-line or multiline text input with optional label, description, and error message. Use it in forms for short answers (email, search, name) or longer content (comments). It supports optional leading and trailing text adornments (e.g. currency or units)."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"Features"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#default","content":"Default"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-controlled","content":"Text Field Controlled"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-invalid","content":"Text Field Invalid"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-disabled","content":"Text Field Disabled"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-adornments","content":"Text Field Adornments"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-multiline","content":"Text Field Multiline"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#props","content":"Props"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Label, description, error**: Optional label, helper text, and error message with proper accessibility"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Adornments**: Optional `leadingText` and `trailingText` for fixed text before or after the input (e.g. `$`, `.00`, `px`)"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Multiline**: Set `multiline` to render a textarea instead of a single-line input"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with `errorMessage` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria TextField for accessibility and behavior"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with label and placeholder."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"1214":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with `errorMessage` for validation feedback."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent input."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-adornments","content":"Use `leadingText` and `trailingText` for fixed text before and after the input, such as currency."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#text-field-multiline","content":"Use `multiline` to render a textarea."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `md` and `sm` visual sizes."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#props","content":"The `TextField` component accepts the following props:"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"page","content":"TextLockup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-0","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup","content":"TextLockup stacks an eyebrow, title, and body text as one coordinated type group across six sizes."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-1","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"Features"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-2","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#installation","content":"Installation"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-3","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#examples","content":"Examples"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-4","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#default","content":"Default"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-5","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-6","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#tag-eyebrow","content":"Tag Eyebrow"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-7","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#alignment","content":"Alignment"},"1229":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-8","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#legible-lines","content":"Legible Lines"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-9","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#with-actions","content":"With Actions"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-10","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"Customization"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-11","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-12","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-13","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#props","content":"Props"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-14","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"Six coordinated sizes, from a `2xl` page title down to `xs`"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-15","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"An eyebrow that takes plain text or a `Tag`, sized to match the lockup"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-16","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"Any heading level, chosen independently of the visual size"},"1238":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-17","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"Start or center alignment"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-18","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"A legible line-length clamp, on by default"},"1240":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-19","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#features","content":"The title steps down a tier in narrow containers"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-20","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#default","content":"A lockup stacks an optional eyebrow, a title and body text as one coordinated type\ngroup. You supply the parts, so the title can be any heading level and the body any\nnumber of paragraphs; `size` sets the tier for all of them at once."},"1242":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-21","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#sizes","content":"`size` is the tier: the eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`,\nand the body on `body`. Use `2xl` for a page title, `xl` for a hero, `lg` for a section\ntitle, and `md` (the default) everywhere else."},"1243":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-22","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#tag-eyebrow","content":"The eyebrow takes either plain text or a `Tag`. Both use `slot=\"eyebrow\"`, so the two\nforms swap freely, and the lockup pairs the tag's `size` with its own."},"1244":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-23","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#alignment","content":"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."},"1245":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-24","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#legible-lines","content":"The text parts are constrained to a comfortable line length by default. Set\n`legibleLines={false}` to let them run the full width of their container, which suits a\nlockup already inside a narrow column. Both lockups below share one wide container, so the\nclamp is what makes the first one narrower."},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-25","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#with-actions","content":"Because you compose the parts, anything else can sit alongside them — a call to action\nhere. Controls keep their own type: the buttons are unaffected by the lockup's `size`."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-26","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-27","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**The body is a bare `<Text>`.** `slot=\"description\"` is equivalent, for consistency with\n`Field` and `Modal`."},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-28","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**The eyebrow is `slot=\"eyebrow\"`**, on either a `Text` or a `Tag`. The two forms swap\nfreely, and a `Tag` is sized to pair with the lockup."},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-29","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**The title is a `Heading`.** Pick the level from the document outline, not the visual size:\n`size` handles the visuals, so `<Heading level={1}>` in an `xs` lockup is perfectly valid."},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-30","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**An explicit prop on a child always wins** over what the lockup supplies. Pass\n`<Tag slot=\"eyebrow\" size=\"sm\">` to break the pairing, for instance."},"1252":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-31","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**Controls keep their own type.** A `Button` inside a lockup is sized by its own `size` prop,\nnot the lockup's."},"1253":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-32","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"**`size` is the tier.** The eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`, and\nthe body on `body`, so there is no table to memorize."},"1254":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-33","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#customization","content":"Pass `className` to extend the styles, or select on `[data-size]` and `[data-align]`."},"1255":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-34","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#accessibility","content":"The title carries the heading semantics. Choose `level` so the page outline stays correct\nrather than to achieve a size."},"1256":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-35","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#accessibility","content":"Slots resolve against the lockup, so `slot=\"title\"` names the lockup's title. Inside a\n`Modal`, `Drawer` or `Popover`, give the dialog its own `<Heading slot=\"title\">` as a direct\nchild for the accessible name, and use the lockup for the body."},"1257":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-36","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#accessibility","content":"The eyebrow is decorative in most designs. If it carries meaning, make sure the title still\nreads sensibly on its own, since screen reader users often navigate by heading."},"1258":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-37","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#best-practices","content":"Use one `2xl` lockup per page at most — it is the page title."},"1259":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-38","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#best-practices","content":"Keep `legibleLines` on for running prose. Turn it off only when the lockup already sits in a\nnarrow column, where the clamp does nothing but complicate the layout."},"1260":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-39","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#best-practices","content":"Prefer a `Tag` eyebrow for status or category, and plain text for a kicker or section label."},"1261":{"id":"/docs/components/text-lockup-40","page_id":"/docs/components/text-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-lockup#best-practices","content":"Reach for `MetricsLockup` instead when the emphasis is a single number rather than prose."},"1262":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"page","content":"ToggleButton","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button"},"1263":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-0","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toggle-button","content":"Accessible toggle button component for grouped contextual actions with single or multiple selection, keyboard navigation, and RTL-aware layouts."},"1264":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-1","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#installation","content":"Installation"},"1265":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-2","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#examples","content":"Examples"},"1266":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-3","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#default","content":"Default"},"1267":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-4","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#multiple-selection","content":"Multiple Selection"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-5","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-6","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#disabled-states","content":"Disabled States"},"1270":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-7","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-8","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-9","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/components/toggle-button-10","page_id":"/docs/components/toggle-button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toggle-button#with-d